     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is my rosemary turning brown and dying from the bottom up?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Rosemary that browns from the base while the mix is damp usually has root rot from too much water or poor drainage. NC State Extension calls overwatering the common cause of rosemary decline and lists root rot as a common disease, and the RHS says cold, wet compost can rot the roots."
