    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can rosemary grow near the sea in the UAE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. NC State Extension describes rosemary as highly salt and drought tolerant, so it suits coastal gardens and balconies. Give it full sun and good air flow, because still, humid air brings powdery mildew."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does rosemary flower, and does it attract bees?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, rosemary flowers. NC State Extension says the tiny flowers are blue, lavender or white (pink in some cultivars) and attract butterflies and bees. NC State gives spring into summer for flowering; UF/IFAS says rosemary in Florida's warm climate blooms in winter and spring."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is rosemary now called Salvia rosmarinus?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Botanists moved rosemary from the old genus Rosmarinus into Salvia, the sage genus, so its accepted name is now Salvia rosmarinus. Rosmarinus officinalis is the former name and is still common on labels. Both names mean the same plant, a member of the mint family (Lamiaceae)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How is plant size measured?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Size is measured from the bottom of the nursery pot to the top tip of the highest leaf. A plant listed as 50-60 CM stands in that range measured this way."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Which pot option should I choose, nursery or decorative?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Choose the nursery pot for the lowest price or if you already have a planter. Choose a decorative pot for a ready-to-display plant that arrives fully potted with soil mix, perlite and a drainage layer. The plant itself is the same."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Do the decorative pots have drainage holes?",
